# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rust's scratch folder. On this project it grows to tens of gigabytes
# (over 56 GB during a release build). It is regenerated by `cargo build`
# and must never be committed.
target/
**/target/

# ── Packaged releases ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The portable Windows folder and its ZIP are built from the source; they are
# not source. A release is attached to a GitHub "Release", not committed.
dist/
*.zip

# ── Compiled binaries and debug symbols ─────────────────────────────────────
# The debug build alone is 511 MB of exe plus 563 MB of .pdb.
*.pdb
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.obj
*.ilk
*.exp

# ── Editor and operating-system noise ───────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Local logs and crash dumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.dmp

# ── ArtCraft trademark assets ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# EffectCraft's docs/brand/LICENSE-brand.txt forbids shipping the ArtCraft
# name, wordmark and logos in a modified or derived product. They stay on the
# author's machine and are not published here.
creativecraft/*/docs/brand/

# ── CreativeCraft's own saved design ────────────────────────────────────────
# Written next to the binary while the window runs; it is the user's work, not
# source.
creativecraft/studio-shell/creativecraft.ccproj
creativecraft/studio-shell/creativecraft.assets/
